{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1a7c0de-uc4-inc-resp-0001-000000000001",
    "name": "Incident Response Service (UC4)",
    "description": "Drives the incident-response process end to end and covers every decision path.\n\nFolder 1 raises an incident, one request per classification scenario; each saves {{incidentId}}.\nFolder 3 lists and completes human tasks using one shared body (extra variables are ignored, so\nthe same body works for any task). Folder 4 has the exact form fields per task if you'd rather\ndemo it properly. Folder 5 is the error responses.\n\nHappy path: raise a P1, wait ~25-30s for the automated chain to reach the human tasks, list active\ntasks (saves {{taskKey}} and {{taskKey2}}), then complete. The parallel phase has two tasks open at\nonce so use both keys; everything after it has one, so 'Complete active task' is enough. Re-list\nbetween phases until it comes back empty, then check the incident is CLOSED.\n\nPhase order: [Containment + Forensic] -> CISO Review -> Integrity Verification -> File Regulatory\nNotification -> Incident Closure.\n\nResponses are wrapped in {\"data\":..., \"meta\":...}; errors are RFC 7807 problem details.\n{{baseUrl}} defaults to http://localhost:8080.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "incidentId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "taskKey",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "taskKey2",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "unknownIncidentId",
      "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
